rl":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This experiment composes PR #5 and PR #6 without changing either implementation or ERC-8404 Core. It independently verifies native replay and authenticated artifact review over the same proof bytes, then recomputes the scoped decision at consumer admission.\n\nThe branch starts from PR #6 and imports 18 additive PR #5 files byte-for-byte. The new claim is a laboratory conjunction; distinct subject labels, original canonicalization rules and authority scopes remain explicit.\n\nLocal replay: 61 scenarios (2 positive, 59 negative/unsupported), 16 tests in normal/repeat/Python -O, 22 killed joint mutations, and 20 separate record-admission controls. Exact A/B/C/D comparison results are in evidence/integration/summary.json. These are finite controls, not general security claims.\n\nOriginal PR #6 16/1 mutation evidence is preserved. An additional witness kills the canonical-byte-carrier fallback; it retains a parsed preimage and does not show authorization without any preimage. Native Rust was rebuilt and replayed; Python/TypeScript Core conformance and independent EIP-712 recovery pass. The initial invalid unsigned-field negative-test premise and its correction are retained in the logs.\n\nThe complete external chain remains PARTIAL_CHAIN_VERIFIED. Missing external input admission, deployed model authority, linked judgment/execution evidence and real-world controller authority are explicit. No production-readiness or upstream vulnerability claim.\n\nSee research/integration/ for source graph, compatibility, trust boundaries, mutation evidence, results, limitations and review checklist. Published-commit fresh replay and CI are required before the final bounded review verdict.\n\n**Draft research only. Do not merge. Existing PR #2-#6 remain unchanged.**\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-20T10:34:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:13Z","closed_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:13Z","merged_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:13Z","merge_commit_sha":"c93087f06bd14c45a1d12b0c068195e3bef05dae","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"trustless-ai:research/claim-aware-composition-integration","ref":"research/claim-aware-composition-integration","repo":{"id":1422280233,"node_id":"R_kgDOVMZGKQ","name":"verifiable-execution-claim-authorization","full_name":"trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization","owner":{"login":"trustless-ai","id":295405515,"node_id":"O_kgDOEZuHyw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/295405515?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustless-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Experimental research on guarantee preservation across verifiable AI inference, attestations, execution receipts, and downstream claims.","homepage":null,"language":"Python","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":1,"fo